From c3ce60e251027851c6c3c3d33d691a939e1938b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:50:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] PDP11 DMP/DMV: maintenance message while starting or
 running reported as 012 (known issue 128)

The DDCMP rules for a maintenance message in Run, ISTRT and ASTRT run
ResetVariables (state Halt) before NotifyMaintRcvd, so the DMP/DMV
translation always reported 014 (received while halted) instead of 012
(now in maintenance state, buffers returned).  VMS then never served a
Request Program the PDP-11 sent on its own (BOOT DMVn).  The dispatcher
keeps the state a rule fired in and the translation uses it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SuavtcpUxEC2vXhit3JaAg
