From 863b003efd09644f401a553866b9bed51b8c58c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:44:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] PDP11 DUP: BOOT DUPn answers Enter MOP Mode and MOP code
 12 at once (known issue 129)

Over a DMF32 (software DDCMP) VMS switches the circuit to maintenance
on the first Request Program, sends MOP code 12 and waits for a new
request for its service timer (4 s).  The bootstrap repeated its
request only after 5 s, so on a slow PDP-11 (11/84 in the realism mode)
VMS gave up: Receive error, Line communication error.  The bootstrap
now repeats its last message at once on code 12 and on Enter MOP Mode;
other messages (e.g. a DECnet routing message over a DMC11) are still
ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SuavtcpUxEC2vXhit3JaAg
